{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01QngY7umoGyTQiGnuMgWqek","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_017pDeUq8kXqEhE8zK751CnP","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat > /tmp/search_results.txt << 'EOF'\nSEARCH RESULTS: submit_dream_review_report Function\n=====================================================\n\nFOUND: YES - Tool exists and is fully implemented\n\nLOCATION 1: Core Implementation\nFile: /home/ubuntu/agent-ml-research/core/tools/feishu_group.py\nLines: 1244-1351\nType: Core function implementation\n\nFunction Signature:\n  def submit_dream_review_report(\n      report: str,\n      project: str,\n      tier: str,\n      dream_id: str,\n      overall_score: str = \"\",\n      review_chat_id: str = \"\",\n      review_visible: bool = True,\n  ) -> ToolResult\n\nKey Features:\n  - Persists Dream-mode review reports to:\n    dream_reports/{dream_id}/{tier}/review_report.md\n  - Adds YAML frontmatter with dream_id, tier, overall_score, timestamp\n  - Optional Group C visibility posting with [Dream Review Report] card\n  - Does NOT send to Research Director or create review_issues.yaml\n  - Normalizes dream_id (strips/adds \"dream_\" prefix as needed)\n  - Returns ToolResult with report_path, dream_id, tier, review_visible\n\nLOCATION 2: MCP Tool Registration\nFile: /home/ubuntu/agent-ml-research/core/mcp_server.py\nLines: 4912-4955\nType: @mcp.tool() decorated wrapper\n\nFunction Signature (MCP wrapper):\n  @mcp.tool()\n  def submit_dream_review_report(\n      report: str,\n      project: str,\n      tier: str,\n      dream_id: str,\n      overall_score: str = \"\",\n      review_chat_id: str = \"\",\n      review_visible: bool = True,\n  ) -> str\n\nPurpose: Exposes the core function as an MCP tool accessible to Claude sessions\n\nLOCATION 3: Tool Registry\nFile: /home/ubuntu/agent-ml-research/core/tool_registry.py\nLine: 477\nTool Set: _DREAM_REVIEW_DIRECTOR_TOOLS (frozenset with 5 tools)\n\nTools in DREAM_REVIEW_DIRECTOR_TOOLS:\n  1. director_post_to_reviewer\n  2. submit_dream_review_report  ← TARGET TOOL\n  3. director_get_project_overview\n  4. read_local_file\n  5. read_project_file\n\nAccess Control:\n  - Accessible to: dream_review_director role ONLY\n  - NOT accessible to: normal review_director or other roles\n  - Used by: Dream-mode Review Director subprocess only\n\nLOCATION 4: MCP Configuration\nFile: /home/ubuntu/agent-ml-research/core/session_server.py\nLine: 305-315 (_ensure_dream_review_director_mcp_config function)\nLine: 941, 948, 969\n\nPurpose: Creates MCP config restricted to DREAM_REVIEW_DIRECTOR_TOOLS\nContext: Called when spawning Dream Review Director subprocess\n\nLOCATION 5: Usage in Dream Pipeline\nFile: /home/ubuntu/agent-ml-research/core/tools/dream.py\nLines: 1035-1041 (in _build_dream_review_dispatch_prompt)\n\nHow it's called:\n  - Dream Review Director subprocess must call this function\n  - Function call is mentioned in the boot prompt sent to subprocess\n  - Example from prompt:\n    submit_dream_review_report(report, project=\"...\", tier=\"...\", \n                              dream_id=\"...\", review_visible=...)\n\nData Flow:\n  1. Dream Pipeline calls _submit_to_review()\n  2. _submit_to_review() spawns Review Director subprocess\n  3. Review Director subprocess calls submit_dream_review_report()\n  4. Report is written to disk at: projects/{project}/artifacts/dream_reports/{dream_id}/{tier}/review_report.md\n  5. Dream Pipeline reads the file after subprocess exits\n  6. Report is included in meta.yaml and DreamOutput\n\nDESIGN CONSTRAINTS (from DREAM_FEEDBACK_ACTION_PROTOCOL.md):\n  - Different from submit_review_report_to_research_director\n  - Skips 5-step protocol (no action matrix, no issue tracking)\n  - Doesn't update review_issues.yaml\n  - Doesn't send to Research Director (orchestrator reads file directly)\n  - Optionally posts Group C visibility card with [Dream] prefix\n  - Used ONLY in Dream-mode Review Director, not in normal Review\n\nCALLER REQUIREMENTS:\n  - Must be called from Dream Review Director subprocess\n  - Must have access to project files\n  - Must provide complete review report (consolidated from reviewers)\n  - dream_id can be with or without \"dream_\" prefix (normalized internally)\n  - tier must be one of: \"best\", \"median\", \"worst\"\n  - Returns ToolResult indicating success/failure + file path\n\nRELATED FUNCTIONS:\n  - _run_dream_review_director_subprocess() - spawns Review Director\n  - _submit_to_review() - orchestrates review for one tier\n  - _build_dream_review_dispatch_prompt() - prepares prompt with tool call\n  - _ensure_dream_review_director_mcp_config() - restricts MCP tools\n\nFILES REFERENCING THIS TOOL:\n  1. /home/ubuntu/agent-ml-research/core/tools/feishu_group.py (definition)\n  2. /home/ubuntu/agent-ml-research/core/mcp_server.py (MCP registration)\n  3. /home/ubuntu/agent-ml-research/core/tool_registry.py (role-based access)\n  4. /home/ubuntu/agent-ml-research/core/session_server.py (MCP config)\n  5. /home/ubuntu/agent-ml-research/core/tools/dream.py (usage in prompt)\n  6. /home/ubuntu/agent-ml-research/docs/plans/DREAM_FEEDBACK_ACTION_PROTOCOL.md (design docs)\n  7. /home/ubuntu/agent-ml-research/docs/plans/DREAM_AGENT_DESIGN.md (architecture docs)\n\nTESTING:\n  - Test files: tests/test_dream_review_*.py\n  - E2E tests verify subprocess exit triggers file read\n  - Tests validate YAML frontmatter generation\n  - Tests verify Group C visibility post when enabled\n\nSTATUS: FULLY IMPLEMENTED AND OPERATIONAL\nEOF\ncat /tmp/search_results.txt\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":240,"cache_read_input_tokens":92308,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":240,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"con